[729.23308, "o", "f the Earth that supports all forms of life, and it is primarily affected by ex\r\n    B. The biosphere is a small part of the Earth's ecosystems, and it is not significantly impacted by human acti\r\n    C. The biosphere is a vital component of the Earth's ecosystems, and it is primarily affected by greenhouse ga\r\n    D. The biosphere is a layer of the Earth that is not essential for life, and it has no impact on the Earth's e\r\nA | Which proteins and biomolecules were added to the synthetic cell model to facilitate cellular deformation and understand the functions of complex cell\r\n    A. Myosin, actin filaments, and anillin.\r\n    B. Myosin, actin filaments, and keratin.\r\n    C. Myosin, collagen, and anillin.\r\n    D. Myosin, actin filaments, and collagen.\r\nD | Which factors and processes play a role in the recognition and signaling between bacteria and eukaryotic host organisms during symbiosis?\r\n    A. RNA polymerase and sigma factors, specifically ECF factors, control gene expression in bacteria during symb\r\n  "]
